From 611eb697cc9b4909af5e5076969e9131e91af4ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lane <lane@local>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 03:16:18 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 27/29] fix: re-freeze the milestone-chain artifact hashes
 again after the integ4 merge

The two lanes/integ4 merges (a6470d4, 0d975a7) brought in MRT typed-emitter
support (N-output emission, emit_typed_cpp.py +292 lines), the julia
uniform fix, corpus driver texture support, and iteration-group wiring --
all of which regenerate src/typed_generated/typed_slice.cpp and
typed_manifest.json for every projection, moving every one of the
milestone-chain artifact hashes this lane had just re-frozen for the
0ed489ec corpus bump (task35, edge/glyph-map, emboss). None of this
touches load_slice's own spec metadata, so every spec-JSON hash from the
prior fix is confirmed unchanged; only the generated-artifact hashes
moved.

Recomputed all of them together in two scripts run directly against the
post-merge tree (not reused from any earlier run): one covers the
emboss181/glitch180/edge179/glyph178/live182 chain end to end, the other
covers glyph_map's scanline177 and task35's 176/175-program projections.
Cross-checked internally: edge_bvec3's edge179/glyph178 and glyph_map's
glyph178 pull the identical values the emboss script computed for the
same milestones (same exclusion-set composition, three independent call
sites agreeing), and task35's own bitwise-key block hash and catalog.hpp
across every state came back byte-identical to the pre-merge run,
confirming the two lanes' change set genuinely does not touch those and
this is not a blind swap of numbers.

Re-pinned: test_task35_bitwise_number_profile.py (2 hashes),
test_edge_bvec3_contour.py (2 states x 2 artifacts),
test_glyph_map_nonnegative_int_shift.py (2 states x 2 artifacts),
test_emboss_color_style.py (5 states x 2 artifacts; catalog.hpp
untouched throughout, matching the cross-check above). Ran all four
modules together: 50 tests, OK (skipped=7, all authority-gated).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
